---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import HudTile from '../components/HudTile.astro';
import StatusChit from '../components/StatusChit.astro';
---

<Site
  title="Face tracking"
  description="Light, local face tracking for your Vellum HUD: widgets anchored to your face, running on your machine, off by default."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Light face tracking</p>
        <h1>Widgets that<br /><em>find your face.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Widgets can follow you instead of sitting in a corner: your conditions ride above your
          head, your nameplate sits under your chin. Lean out of frame and they slide back to their
          fixed spots.
        </p>
        <div class="status-line" style="margin-top: 1.25rem">
          <StatusChit status="live" />
          <span class="small">Off by default. Every frame works without it.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <HudTile anchors condition="" caption="Face anchor · demo" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="light-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Light, on purpose</p>
        <h2 id="light-h">It finds where your face is. That's all.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Vellum uses a small face detector: a box around your face and six points. It doesn't read
          expressions, it doesn't recognise who you are, and it never changes your stats.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Small</h3>
          <p class="small">
            The model is about 230 KB and runs a few milliseconds per frame on a normal CPU.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Smooth</h3>
          <p class="small">
            It checks your position about 15 times a second, and widgets glide between checks so
            they don't jitter.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Idle when unused</h3>
          <p class="small">
            If no widget in your frame is anchored to your face, the detector doesn't run at all.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="local-h">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">Strictly local</p>
        <h2 id="local-h">Camera frames never leave your machine.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          With tracking on, the Vellum page inside OBS opens your webcam itself, draws it, finds
          your face and lays the HUD on top, all in one place. The model is served from vellumhud.com
          with the app, never from a third party, and nothing is sent back.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="chain">
        <li><b>Webcam</b><span>Opened by Vellum</span></li>
        <li class="you"><b>Detector</b><span>On your CPU</span></li>
        <li><b>HUD</b><span>Anchored to you</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="setup-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Setup</p>
        <h2 id="setup-h">One extra step.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          OBS has to be started with camera access for browser sources turned on. The app's setup
          panel spots when it's missing and shows the exact fix for your system.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps three">
        <li>
          <h3>Start OBS with the camera flag</h3>
          <p>Launch OBS with <code>--enable-media-stream</code>. The guide has a shortcut per OS.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Use the camera scene</h3>
          <p>Pick the "Vellum camera" scene, which lets Vellum draw your webcam itself.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Choose a frame with anchors</h3>
          <p>Frames that use face anchors say so in the picker.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/face-tracking/">Face tracking guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
